<overview>
<p>Despite the low regard most Clans hold for conventional infantry, these formations benefit from incidental access to Clan technology that makes even a disaffected garrison Point a match for its Inner Sphere equivalent. Field Gun Points are crew-served weapon teams that bring heavier firepower to the infantry level, towing weapons too large for individual soldiers to carry. The gun itself defines the Point's role, with lighter autocannons providing anti-infantry and anti-vehicle fire while heavier weapons can threaten even armored targets. The Point tows an anti-personnel gauss rifle that uses magnetic acceleration to deliver projectiles at extreme velocity, providing precision anti-infantry fire with no chemical propellant signature.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on General Clan faction intro date. Uses Generic Infantry kit due to much later intro date of standard Clan kit.
</notes>

